{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_qytv6e7ar5e43cjpng33ezie7ixpcnclsye3pyj7uzbgltdtni6q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All tests pass. The C-to-Rust translation is complete:\n\n## Summary\n\nI translated the C carrays library to safe, idiomatic Rust:\n\n**`src/carrays.rs`** — Implemented all generic array utility functions:\n- `gca_roundup32` / `gca_roundup64` — round up to next power of 2 using bit-twiddling (with wrapping arithmetic to handle 0 input)\n- `gca_calc_gcd` — Binary GCD algorithm matching the C version\n- `gca_capacity` — Vec-based capacity growth\n- `gca_swapm` — byte-slice swap using safe `swap_with_slice`\n- `gca_cycle_left` / `gca_cycle_right` — using safe `slice::rotate_left/right`\n- `gca_reverse` — element-wise byte-chunk reversal using `split_at_mut`\n- `gca_is_sorted` / `gca_is_rsorted` — using `windows(2)` iteration\n- `gca_max` / `gca_min` — generic comparison-based min/max returning `Option<&T>`\n\n**`src/circ_array.rs`** — Implemented `CircBuf` matching the C `CircBuf` semantics. Since the struct uses `NonNull<u8>` for the underlying buffer, raw allocation/deallocation requires `unsafe` (analogous to the C `malloc`/`realloc`/`free`). Implemented `new`, `dealloc`, `resize`, `capacity`, `push`, `pop`, `unshift`, `shift`, `norm`, plus a `Drop` impl to ensure memory is freed even if `dealloc()` isn't called.\n\nAll 2 existing tests in `runtests.rs` pass (`test_round`, `test_gcd`)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":816,"cache_read_input_tokens":42086,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":816,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"38e0dcbe-fa42-43b9-9f4f-54005a634076","uuid":"ae2ff5a2-f8ad-4932-aa6b-1d39ad24e267"}
